#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:1
msgid "ADR-0017: Evaluation of the MCP server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P13.8 (REQ-MCP-7)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:9
msgid ""
"The MCP server is useful only if an assistant can reach right results "
"through it. Unit tests call each tool, but do not show that a task stated"
" in plain language (UC1, UC8, UC9) can be solved with the tools, nor that"
" an assistant actually solves it. The answer of an assistant is free "
"text, and its quality changes with the model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:13
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:15
msgid ""
"`lumos.mcp.evaluation` defines **scenarios**: a task in plain language, "
"expected values derived from analytic solutions (Bracewell transmission "
"sin²(π B θ / λ), Gaussian beam radius w(z), Airy ring mean and the "
"rejection of an ideal vortex), and a rule per value (relative or absolute"
" tolerance, upper bound). The task asks the assistant to end with a JSON "
"object of named numbers; `parse_answer` reads the last one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:19
msgid ""
"Each scenario has a **scripted reference solution** that only calls MCP "
"tools. The tests run it through an in-process client and check its answer"
" with the same rules: the scenario is solvable with the tools, and the "
"rules accept a right answer (other tests check that they reject wrong "
"ones)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:22
msgid ""
"The scripted solutions run at every CI run (they are tests): this is the "
"periodic part of REQ-MCP-7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:23
msgid ""
"`run_with_claude_code` gives the task to Claude Code (`claude -p`) with "
"the MCP server of LUMOS as its only tools (`--mcp-config`, `--strict-mcp-"
"config`, `--allowedTools mcp__lumos`) and checks the final answer, read "
"from the JSON output. It runs on demand with the subscription of the "
"user: `tools/mcp_eval.py --claude-code`. Without option, "
"`tools/mcp_eval.py` runs the scripted solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:27
msgid ""
"Missing capabilities found while writing the scenarios became tools: "
"`radial_profile` (contrast in rings) and the 1/e² beam radius in the "
"summaries of fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:30
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:32
msgid ""
"Judging the answers with a language model: not verifiable, and the "
"results have exact physical references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:33
msgid ""
"Running the evaluation with Claude in every CI run: costs and flakiness "
"on every commit; the scripted solutions keep the scenarios honest at no "
"cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:35
msgid ""
"A weekly run through the Claude API (first version of this ADR): needs an"
" API key billed per token, too costly for the project; replaced on "
"2026-10-17 by Claude Code on demand, which uses an existing subscription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:39
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:41
msgid ""
"New use cases join the evaluation as a scenario with an analytic "
"expectation and a scripted solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0017-mcp-evaluation.md:42
msgid ""
"A failure of a run with Claude Code means a regression of the server or "
"of the guidance it gives (instructions, descriptions, hints), or a model "
"that needs better guidance; the report holds the answers."
msgstr ""

